# Zakaa-io — UI/UX Audit & Roadmap

**Generated:** 2026-08-01
**Scope:** Comprehensive UI/UX audit (typography, RTL, color, animations, contrast, usability)

---

## P0 — Critical

### TYPOGRAPHY

- [ ] **Missing type scale system** — No consistent 12/14/16/18/20/24/30/36/48px scale. Implement a CSS custom property-based type scale in `globals.css` and apply consistently across all sections (`Hero.tsx:59`, `SectionHeader.tsx:19`, `Pricing.tsx:115`, etc.).
- [ ] **Inconsistent body text sizing** — Body text uses arbitrary values like `text-sm`, `text-[0.95rem]`, `text-lg`, `text-base` without a defined scale. Normalize to the type scale.
- [ ] **Missing font-weight scale** — Weights are scattered (`font-extrabold`, `font-bold`, `font-semibold`, `font-medium`) without a clear hierarchy map. Document and enforce a weight scale (e.g., 400 body, 500 labels, 600 buttons, 700 headings, 800 display).
- [ ] **Arabic typography** — Arabic text uses the same Inter font. Inter has limited Arabic glyph coverage. Add a dedicated Arabic web font (e.g., `Noto Sans Arabic` or `Cairo`) via `@import` and conditionally apply it when `locale="ar"`.

### RTL LAYOUT & DIRECTIONALITY

- [ ] **RTL positioning bugs** — `BackToTopButton.tsx:48` uses `fixed bottom-6 left-6` which is LTR-only. In RTL mode it should be `right-6`. Same for `AIChatWidget.tsx:111` (`fixed bottom-5 right-5`). Use logical CSS properties or conditional classes.
- [ ] **RTL arrow direction** — `Process.tsx:64` uses `→` which is LTR. In RTL mode it should be `←`. `Phase3Labs.tsx:190` uses `→` in the product card CTA. `Hero.tsx:78` uses `→` in the CTA button.
- [ ] **RTL text alignment** — `AssessmentWizard.tsx:120` and `LeadForm.tsx:63` hardcode `text-left`. In RTL mode these should be `text-right`. The `dir="rtl"` attribute is set on the wizard but `text-left` overrides it.
- [ ] **RTL flex/grid direction** — `Navbar.tsx:133` mobile menu items use `text-left`. `Footer.tsx:69` uses `text-left` for the brand description. `CTA.tsx:75` uses `justify-end` for language toggle which may need RTL adjustment.
- [ ] **RTL border-radius mirroring** — Cards and buttons use asymmetric border-radius values like `rounded-l-[10px]` or directional padding that may not mirror correctly. Audit all directional utilities.

### COLOR CONTRAST (ACCESSIBILITY)

- [ ] **Low contrast muted text** — `#64748B` on `#111827` yields ~4.5:1 (borderline WCAG AA for normal text). On `#06060a` it yields ~3.2:1 (fails WCAG AA). Used in `Footer.tsx:69`, `Testimonials.tsx:66`, `Phase3Labs.tsx:199`, `AIChatWidget.tsx:142`. Increase to `#94A3B8` or darker.
- [ ] **Low contrast secondary text on light surfaces** — `#a1a1aa` on `#e4e4e7` (light mode) yields ~3.5:1. Increase to `#52525b` or darker in light mode.
- [ ] **Accent text on dark background** — `#6366f1` on `#06060a` yields ~5.5:1 (passes AA). `#3B82F6` on `#0F172A` yields ~4.8:1 (passes AA but borderline for large text). Document contrast ratios in a style guide.
- [ ] **Ghost button contrast** — `text-[#a1a1aa]` on transparent/bg surface with border may not meet 3:1 for UI components. Increase to `#94A3B8`.

### GENERAL USABILITY

- [ ] **Mobile menu focus trap incomplete** — `Navbar.tsx:58-89` handles Escape and Tab cycling, but doesn't trap focus within the menu when opened. Implement a proper focus trap using `focus()` calls or a library.
- [ ] **Mobile menu outside click** — Clicking outside the mobile menu doesn't close it. Add a backdrop or document click handler.
- [ ] **Missing skip link styling** — `layout.tsx:53-58` has a skip link but it only appears on focus. Consider making it always visible with low opacity for better discoverability.
- [ ] **Form labels missing visible text** — `LeadForm.tsx:71-107` uses `aria-label` but no visible `<label>` elements. Add visible labels above inputs for better UX and accessibility.
- [ ] **Assessment wizard step indicator** — `AssessmentWizard.tsx:234` shows "Step X/3" but lacks proper ARIA (`aria-current`, `aria-valuenow`). Add step indicator with progress semantics.
- [ ] **Button type inconsistencies** — Some buttons in `Navbar.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`, and `CTA.tsx` lack explicit `type="button"`, causing potential form submission issues when nested in forms.

